    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the draft is good but honestly i'm a bit worried about how to describe the extra tasks. it feels like they're just slowly sneaking in and making the project way bigger than it should be. how can i explain that \"scope creep\" is actually making it impossible to hit our original dates without sounding like i'm just making excuses?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can frame it as the *rate* of change impacting the original estimates, rather than blaming the changes themselves. Instead of saying \"scope creep,\" use more objective language that points to the volume of new work.\n\nTry phrasing it like this: \"The iterative nature of the requirements gathering has resulted in a significant accumulation of new, high-priority tasks that were outside the initial project charter.\"\n\nThis sounds far more like a technical assessment than a complaint. It acknowledges the process while clearly stating the impact on the timeline. It's a subtle way of saying, \"The requirements are growing faster than we can build them.\"",
      "source": "target",
